# ButterPOS Coding Standards

## Stack & style
- Python 3.11+, FastAPI, **async-first**. Type hints on every function. Pydantic v2 for all models.
- No business logic in route handlers — routes call **services**; services are testable in isolation.
- All endpoints under `/api/v1/`.

## Provider isolation (the core architectural rule)
- The middleware core NEVER imports a platform SDK. All ticketing goes through the **`TicketingProvider`** interface; Chatwoot is one adapter (`ChatwootAdapter`). A future `ZohoAdapter` must slot in with zero core changes.
- The core NEVER imports a vendor LLM SDK (`openai`, `google-generativeai`, `anthropic`, etc.). All model calls go through the **`LLMProvider`** interface. Adding/swapping a provider (incl. future Ollama) is config, not new plumbing.
- Tool calls go through the **MCP client** layer. Adding a new tool must NOT require touching the agent loop (the "Super Agent" must stay extensible).

## Reliability
- Every external call (platform API, LLM API, MCP) is wrapped with timeout, retry, and structured logging.
- Log every request with timestamp, `user_id`, `ticket_id`. Use a global exception handler.

## Security
- Secrets only from env via `pydantic-settings`. Never hardcoded, never logged, never committed.
- **PII masking is mandatory before any LLM call** in V1 (data goes to third-party paid providers). Masks are reversible via Redis (24h TTL).
- Tiered authorization: Tier 1 read-only auto; Tier 2 fix on high-confidence / soft-confirm otherwise; Tier 3 always escalate.

## Testing
- Every new module ships with tests.
- Customer/branch mapping logic requires **100% coverage** (active plan, expired, unpaid, 8h/16h/24-7, unknown user, no branch). Show coverage output at the gate.
